   "html_text": "Time-slice theories have some assets. For one, they are relatively simple. On a time-slice theory, what explains a subject’s justification at a time is just the way things are then. It is more complicated to identify the way things are at other times as also being relevant. Moreover, the way things are at a time might fully explain a subject’s justification then. For example, a subject’s recollective dispositions and what she seems to recollect at a time might account for all her justification f",
